{
  "_comment": [
    "Maps each SVG in the coral folder to how the corridor should use it.",
    "Drop a new .svg in the folder, add an entry here, and re-run build_corridor.py.",
    "  name   : growth form, for documentation only",
    "  scale  : relative size in the scene. 1.0 is a typical head-sized colony;",
    "           a whole reef clump is larger, a single tuft smaller.",
    "  detail : 'chunky' shapes hold up at distance. 'fine' shapes have strokes",
    "           that fall below one pixel far away and shimmer, so they are only",
    "           placed near the camera.",
    "Files are used as CSS masks, so their own fill colours are ignored and the",
    "silhouette colour is set by the scene (it lightens with distance)."
  ],
